  "description_short": "Traditional South African fare in a warm village inn setting near Tsitsikamma's forests and trails.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into the heart of Storms River village, De Oude Martha serves hearty, home-style cooking that welcomes hungry adventurers after a day exploring Tsitsikamma. The restaurant is part of the historic Tsitsikamma Village Inn, offering a cosy, unpretentious atmosphere that feels like dining in someone's well-loved country kitchen.\n\nThe menu leans into South African comfort food — think bobotie, oxtail, and generous grills — alongside lighter options for those who've just conquered the suspension bridge or canopy tours. Portions are generous and prices fair, making it a solid choice for families and groups refuelling between outdoor activities.\n\nThe setting is relaxed and welcoming, with a fireplace for chilly evenings and friendly service that knows the area well. It's the kind of place where locals and visitors mix easily, swapping trail stories over a good meal before an early night ahead of tomorrow's adventures.",
